  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CDT WED OCT 28 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery early this afternoon reveals an upper level\nridge breaking down across the Southeast as a shortwave lifts\nacross the Northern Plains, leading to a west-southwest flow\naloft as we head into the weekend. Over the next couple of days,\nTropical Storm Vance will move inland over the west coast of\nMexico. Moisture associated with this system will spread over the\nmountainous terrain of Mexico, eventually across the Plains and\ninto the Southeast by the weekend. We will see rain chances\nreturn to Central Alabama over the weekend as the remnants of\nVance pass near the region. Our greatest rain chances look to\nhold off until Saturday evening, lingering through Sunday\nmorning. There remains some uncertainty as to the exact time of\nthe onset of precipitation, leading to a low chance for some damp\ntrick-or-treating.\n\nWe will have a dry start to the next work week as weak ridging\nbuilds in. We will need to keep a close eye on the upper level\npattern towards the middle of next week. Latest trends hint at\nadditional chances for showers and storms by the middle of the\nweek. Details will be worked out over the coming days.\n\nOtherwise, light winds and clear skies will promote patchy river\nfog during the overnight and early morning hours for the next\ncouple of days.\n\n95/Castillo",
